  "use": "Applied by the comparator (CNF-04) to the reference side of an observation before comparison, entry by entry and only in the entry's scope. An entry without a new value renames nothing until naming.md settles it. A proposed value is carried as proposed, never as decided, and is never applied: only decided and mechanical entries rename the reference side, and a difference a proposed entry would explain is reported annotated with that entry's deviation. Engine-interface names that pass through verbatim (naming.md section 3.4) are not renamed, so there is no blanket MAYA_ prefix rule. Section 3.10 lists planner names, not donor names, and has no entry here. Read and checked by console-conformance::scenario::RenameMap; a test checks every entry and exclusion against naming.md and every deviation id against deviations.md.",
